subject: fix(smart-router): 4 real bugs caught by production E2E testing

The smart router never actually worked end-to-end before this commit.
Browser testing with a real request exposed each failure in sequence:

1. Enumeration bug (silent no-op): resolveSmartRouter iterated PROVIDERS,
   which is TRANSPORT-ONLY (baseUrl/format) — providerDef.models was always
   undefined, so zero candidates and the router always fell through.
   Now iterates PROVIDER_MODELS (alias-keyed) and maps alias -> canonical
   provider id via PROVIDER_ID_TO_ALIAS.

2. Combo-reuse crash: getOrCreateSmartCombo ran JSON.parse(existing.models)
   but combosRepo returns models as an ALREADY-PARSED array -> threw on
   second request reusing an existing sr- combo. Guard added.

3. Sticky-session corruption: open-sse setStickySession(messages, provider,
   model) stores {provider, model}; the app-layer wrapper passed the combo
   name as the whole value and returned the raw object, so the second turn
   of a conversation got comboName: {provider: "sr-..."}. Wrapper now stores
   the combo name in the provider slot and reads entry.provider back.

4. Crash on first successful resolve: chat.js declared `const modelStr` but
   the interception assigned modelStr = comboName -> TypeError 500. Now let.

Verified E2E (production standalone build): POST modelRouter ->
"sr-modelRouter-code-generation" created with 3 real scored models
(antigravity/claude-sonnet-4-6, blackbox/claude-opus-4.8, ...), fallback
chain tried each in order with per-attempt status/latency in the error
body, combo visible with capability badges in the dashboard.

Tests: tests/unit/smart-router-resolve.test.js — 5 tests (candidate
selection from PROVIDER_MODELS, combo content, allowedProviders filter,
disabled/non-trigger null, concurrency decrement). All pass. Full suite:
1685 passed / 88 failed (pre-existing baseline only).

Part of: Smart Router & Fallback UX plan (Phase 1 fixes)


